1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,666
Learn any movement
from a single recording.

2
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:09,815
You follow a video, and nobody
tells you what your copy got wrong.

3
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:15,924
One teacher records a movement once.

4
00:00:15,964 --> 00:00:18,487
That recording is all Simon needs.

5
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:27,408
It becomes a 3D movement that anyone
can open, and turn to any angle.

6
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:34,471
Anyone can follow it.

7
00:00:34,511 --> 00:00:36,632
They film their own copy on a phone.

8
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:43,307
Now the wait.

9
00:00:43,347 --> 00:00:47,524
The analysis took
3 minutes 27 seconds on the GPU.

10
00:00:47,564 --> 00:00:49,211
Here it is, sped up.

11
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:57,360
Under the hood, SAM 3.1 tracks the person.

12
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:00,809
Muse Spark finds the sections
of the movement.

13
00:01:00,849 --> 00:01:04,784
SAM 3D Body, built on DINOv3,
lifts the pose into 3D.

14
00:01:04,824 --> 00:01:07,633
Then Simon compares the two skeletons,

15
00:01:07,673 --> 00:01:11,608
and Muse Spark puts the differences
into plain words.

16
00:01:12,598 --> 00:01:16,319
Here is SAM 3D Body
at work on two stock clips.

17
00:01:20,598 --> 00:01:21,580
The result:

18
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:23,718
77 out of 100, grade C.

19
00:01:27,598 --> 00:01:31,500
The 3D view lays the copy
over the teacher, so you can turn it

20
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:33,853
and see exactly where the two differ.

21
00:01:39,598 --> 00:01:41,282
And the cue is timed.

22
00:01:41,322 --> 00:01:44,155
Keep your chest up, at 0.9 seconds.

23
00:01:47,598 --> 00:01:51,920
Simon tells shape from timing,
and replays your worst moment on a loop.

24
00:01:56,598 --> 00:02:01,834
A clip to share is one tap away, and a card
shows which Meta models made each step.

25
00:02:08,598 --> 00:02:10,246
Dance, rehab or fitness:

26
00:02:10,286 --> 00:02:13,834
one capability for any movement
a teacher can show.

27
00:02:18,598 --> 00:02:23,787
This is Simon, built on Meta's
SAM 3.1, SAM 3D Body and Muse Spark.

28
00:02:23,827 --> 00:02:27,300
The code was written
in the hackathon window.

29
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:31,593
The footage is one real,
cleared take plus stock clips.
